---
# Stricter clang-tidy for the project-model library (deluge::project).
#
# This is greenfield, idiomatic-C++26 code (the boundary the project-model
# extraction is building), so it holds itself to a higher bar than the legacy
# tree. It inherits the repo-root .clang-tidy (naming conventions — lower_case
# variables/members, kCamelCase constants — and the bulk of the checks) and adds
# the checks the root leaves off for the legacy code but which new code here can
# and should satisfy:
#
#   * modernize-avoid-c-arrays            — prefer std::array/std::span (the
#       cppcoreguidelines twin is already on repo-wide; this is the modernize one).
#   * cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions — rule of 0/5 for the value types.
#   * cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables — no mutable globals in
#       the model library.
#
# Naming (lower_case variables/members, kCamelCase constants) is inherited from
# root and is the target for new code in this library.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions,
  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
